{"type":"text","timestamp":1787443573222,"sessionID":"ses_fd40febdbffeutsjoBqRpIpPPf","part":{"id":"prt_02bf06c5e001nMFClLvGwdfdFd","messageID":"msg_02bf069bd001yWM3ip0buOZdro","sessionID":"ses_fd40febdbffeutsjoBqRpIpPPf","type":"text","text":"Implemented the comparison-summary feature and added tests.\n\nDesign:\n- `summarize-assistants.mjs`: filters eligible runs (`complete`, `pass`, `comparison_eligible !== false`), validates required fields only for eligible runs, groups by assistant, picks the best run by score → elapsed → run_id, computes median elapsed time, and returns summaries sorted by assistant. The input array and records are never mutated.\n- `render-comparison-table.mjs`: validates every summary, preserves order, renders the exact Markdown header and alignment row, escapes `|` as `\\|`, formats median milliseconds as seconds with three decimals, and shows `_No eligible runs._` for an empty array.\n\nEdge cases covered by added `student-tests.mjs` cases:\n- Invalid eligible runs cause `TypeError` while ineligible runs with invalid data are ignored; input is not mutated.\n- Best-run tie-breaker falls through to lexicographically smaller `run_id` when score and elapsed time are equal.\n- Median for an even number of runs averages the two middle values.\n- `renderComparisonTable` rejects invalid summary fields and preserves the supplied order, including boundary scores and zero elapsed time.\n\nVerification:\n```\nnode --test benchmark/fixtures/T3-comparison-summary/comparison-summary.test.mjs benchmark/fixtures/T3-comparison-summary/student-tests.mjs\n```\nResult: 9/9 tests passed.","time":{"start":1787443571806,"end":1787443573220}}}
